<title>USA: Continental Materials offer terminated.</title>
<headline>Continental Materials offer terminated.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Materials Corp said Tuesday that chairman and chief executive officer James Gidwitz and other members of his family have terminated their offer to acquire the company for $21 a share.</p>
<p>The move came after a special committee of the company's board of directors informed the family the offer was inadequate, the company said.  </p>
<p>Gidwitz also informed the board of directors that the Gidwitz family has not changed its previously announced position against the sale of the company or its assets to any other party, the company said.</p>
<p>In November, the $21 a share offer was made by Gidwitz with the aim of taking the company private.</p>
<p>Continental shares were down 2-3/8 at 21-1/4 Tuesday morning.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
